# Users allowed to ask the Hermes session broker for client accounts.
#
# One name or numeric uid per line; '#' starts a comment. The uid is taken
# from the kernel through SO_PEERCRED, so an entry here grants exactly the
# account that runs Hermes and nobody who can merely reach the socket.
#
# Grant this to the user Hermes runs as. Everything that user can then ask for
# is bounded by the broker's four requests - it cannot name an account, choose
# a uid, or reach outside the session home root.
